{"name":"Spotted Snake Eel","hex":"#b1d3e3","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spotted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Discoloured by spots; stained.","(no comparative or superlative) Characterized by spots (used especially of animals and plants)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of spot"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spotted"},{"term":"snake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the suborder Serpentes of legless reptiles with long, thin bodies and fork-shaped tongues.","A person who acts deceitfully for personal or social gain; a treacherous person."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To follow or move in a winding route.","To steal slyly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snake"},{"term":"eel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any freshwater fish of the order Anguilliformes, which are elongated and resemble snakes.","A European eel (Anguilla anguilla)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fish for eels.","To move with a sinuous motion like that of an eel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spotted snake eel","blocks":[{"text":"There are two species of eel named spotted snake eel:"},{"items":["Myrichthys maculosus","Myrichthys tigrinus"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spotted_snake_eel"},{"title":"Myrichthys maculosus","blocks":[{"text":"Myrichthys maculosus, commonly known as the tiger snake eel, the ocellate snake eel or the spotted snake eel, is a species of fish in the family Ophichthidae, native to the Indo-Pacific. It is occasionally encountered in the aquarium trade. It grows to a length of 1 m (40 in)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Tieso_ocelado_%28Myrichthys_maculosus%29%2C_Zanz%C3%ADbar%2C_Tanzania%2C_2024-05-31%2C_DD_77.jpg/330px-Tieso_ocelado_%28Myrichthys_maculosus%29%2C_Zanz%C3%ADbar%2C_Tanzania%2C_2024-05-31%2C_DD_77.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myrichthys_maculosus"},{"title":"Ophichthidae","blocks":[{"text":"Ophichthidae is a family of fish in the order Anguilliformes, commonly known as the snake eels. The term \"Ophichthidae\" comes from Greek ophis (\"serpent\") and ichthys (\"fish\"). Snake eels are also burrowing eels. They are named for their physical appearance, as they have long, cylindrical, snake-like bodies. This family is found worldwide in tropical to warm temperate waters. They inhabit a wide range of habitats, from coastal shallows and even rivers, to depths below 800 m (2,600 ft). Most species are bottom dwellers, hiding in mud or sand to capture their prey of crustaceans and small fish, but some are pelagic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Aprognathodon_platyventris_-_pone.0010676.g015.png/330px-Aprognathodon_platyventris_-_pone.0010676.g015.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ophichthidae"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Tieso_ocelado_%28Myrichthys_maculosus%29%2C_Zanz%C3%ADbar%2C_Tanzania%2C_2024-05-31%2C_DD_77.jpg/500px-Tieso_ocelado_%28Myrichthys_maculosus%29%2C_Zanz%C3%ADbar%2C_Tanzania%2C_2024-05-31%2C_DD_77.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Tieso_ocelado_%28Myrichthys_maculosus%29%2C_Zanz%C3%ADbar%2C_Tanzania%2C_2024-05-31%2C_DD_77.jpg/1280px-Tieso_ocelado_%28Myrichthys_maculosus%29%2C_Zanz%C3%ADbar%2C_Tanzania%2C_2024-05-31%2C_DD_77.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Tieso_ocelado_%28Myrichthys_maculosus%29%2C_Zanz%C3%ADbar%2C_Tanzania%2C_2024-05-31%2C_DD_77.jpg/500px-Tieso_ocelado_%28Myrichthys_maculosus%29%2C_Zanz%C3%A